Z||000000||mrgone||03-29-2001||01:39 AM||||im 18, im in first year automotive manufacturing, and have wanted a fiero for a long time. people say i may have been blinded when i bought this 1986 2m4 5speed today... it was 1000$ canadian. i didnt negotiate, didnt have it checked out. i got the car from the brother of a friend and when he drove me around in it, it seemed to work fine and i was happy. today i got it home, drove it around a little, it seemed unusually diffacult to drive. stalled it about 6 times, i blamed my lack of stick skill and linkage gear.<BR>i park it and start to look at my new ride, and notice its smoking quite perfusly. it has 230,000 kilometers on it.<BR>things i know is wrong with the car.<BR>headliner<BR>headlight motors<BR>gear linkage<BR>needs a tire (1 is bald)<BR>motor mount<BR>my roomate who is fairly experienced (worked on a 300zx racing team for several years) sais the clutch has been tightened.<BR>now the motor is smoking after minimal usage.<BR>i signed the as-is sale form and i fear i may be screwed. this car could send me into a hell of certification costs, and repair fees. i start work may 14th at a honda assebly plant about 20 mins away, and need some form of reliable transport. im out of student loan and had to borrow against my life insurance to get this car.<BR>its on empty.<BR>has no plates, registration, or insurance until it passes certification.<BR>i live 1600 kms away from my parents.. i fear i should have listened to them. ||||reg||9
